WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.160
But just as I was
giving up hope,

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.600
on the horizon...

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.520
Thank God.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.640
Honestly. Thank God.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.720
(speaking foreign language)

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.040
HAZEN: There they are.
I got them.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.320
It's the camel train.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.560
(camel bellows)

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.600
(man shouting)

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.640
HAZEN: Yes!

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.800
HAZEN: So, this is
the camel train, look at how...

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.360
It's amazing.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.160
Wow, I cannot believe
I found it.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.280
This is...

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.800
HAZEN: ...spectacular!

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:49.840
What's your name?

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.520
HAZEN: Kara Elema. Kara Elema?

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.800
KARA ELEMA: Kara Elema.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.120
HAZEN: He is the leader of
this whole community here,

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.000
and the leader of this caravan,
this big train of camels.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.720
Water! Oh, my god.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.320
Thank you.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.360
(camel bellows)

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.880
Meeting up with these nomads
is a lifesaver.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.400
(camel bellows)

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.800
But we've all still got
quite a journey ahead of us.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.320
(camel bellows)

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.680
Look at this.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.560
All of this that you see right
there, the twigs, the materials,

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.320
the baskets, this is
everything that they own.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.080
This is the, this is
the moving truck right here.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.320
(camel grumbling)

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.320
The Gabra go to
extraordinary lengths,

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.520
traveling for weeks at a time...

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.760
(camel bellowing)

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.920
...moving entire settlements
across the desert

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.800
in search of new grazing grounds
for their herds.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.360
(bellowing)

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.400
They're moving to bigger,
better pastures.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.880
But it's all about being hopeful

00:01:55.880 --> 00:02:01.880
because it hasn't rained here
for so, so long.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.280
So as spectacular
as this whole event is,

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.440
this is an event
out of desperation,

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.680
and yes, there are smiles,

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.280
because people, there is hope
that life will get better

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.920
once they get
to their destination.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:25.320
(grumbling)

